grep - find lines that match

SYNOPSIS
    grep [-i] [-v] [-n] PATTERN [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
      -i   ignore case
      -v   print the lines that do not match
      -n   put the line number in front

    The pattern is a literal string, not a regular expression. That is a real
    limitation and an honest one: a half-implemented regex engine is worse
    than a substring search that says so.

SEE ALSO
    find, sort, uniq
